From 561a0b97ecaca8059185fdf07fbdb1c5a491e6a0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: waydroid-nvidia-prolapse <build@local>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 00:58:18 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 08/24] hwcomposer: check the cursor buffer is importable
 before attaching it
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

What: cursor_handler::create_buffer() runs displayable_buffer() and copies an
unimportable cursor buffer into wl_shm (the path persist.waydroid.
cursor_force_shm already uses) instead of attaching its dma-buf.

Why: get_wl_buffer() skips its displayable_buffer() gate for
HWC_IS_CURSOR_LAYER and hands cursor layers to the cursor handler, which
attached the dma-buf unconditionally. Android's pointer buffers are small and
CPU-written; when one is LINEAR and the compositor imports that format through
NVIDIA's EGL, the attach is a fatal zwp_linux_buffer_params error (source:
"attach dmabuf: 25x32 ... mod 0x0", then wl_display error 7). With the LINEAR
gate (earlier patch) this check is what keeps the cursor path consistent with
every other layer.

Source: QuinOvaX, quinovax/waydroid-nvidia dev ad04e0a
  https://github.com/quinovax/waydroid-nvidia/commit/ad04e0a5c49e3bb48382fa535a6952aaff67b8a6
Licence: Apache-2.0 (android_hardware_waydroid; the fork's patches/hwcomposer/
inherit it).

Deviation from the source: none in behaviour; the fake_touch/mouse_as_touch
cursor hunks of the same commit are input features and not taken.

游标导入检查和 wl_shm 回退使用 ctl 连接；保留 ATV 已有的游标 fence 处理。

(cherry picked from commit d4ed688aff667febd326c75b83f93e4672a058eb)
---
 hwcomposer/hwcomposer.cpp | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/hwcomposer/hwcomposer.cpp b/hwcomposer/hwcomposer.cpp
index 951801e..c1a32b2 100644
--- a/hwcomposer/hwcomposer.cpp
+++ b/hwcomposer/hwcomposer.cpp
@@ -1345,6 +1345,17 @@ static int hwc_open(const struct hw_module_t* module, const char* name,
 }
 
 std::unique_ptr<buffer> cursor_handler::create_buffer(waydroid_hwc_composer_device_1 *pdev, const buffer_metadata& metadata, hwc_layer_1 *hwc_layer) {
+    /* get_wl_buffer() sends cursor layers here without its displayable_buffer() gate, so the
+     * same admission check is made here: a cursor buffer the compositor cannot import (LINEAR on
+     * an NVIDIA-EGL compositor) would be a fatal zwp_linux_buffer_params error. It is copied
+     * into wl_shm instead, the path cursor_force_shm already uses. */
+    if (hwc_layer->handle
+        && !pdev->gralloc_handler.displayable_buffer(pdev->display->ctl.get(), hwc_layer->handle)) {
+        static int count = 0;
+        if ((count++ % 500) == 0)
+            ALOGW("cursor buffer not importable by the compositor; using wl_shm (%d times)", count);
+        return create_shm_wl_buffer(pdev->display->ctl.get(), metadata, hwc_layer->handle);
+    }
     return pdev->gralloc_handler.create_buffer(pdev->display->ctl.get(), metadata, hwc_layer->handle);
 };
 
